    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "---"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793974413995834800",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "3. Delivered Milestones"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1793974413995835300",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "[x] Phase 1: Scaffolding, Core MVP & UI Foundation"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1793974413995835900",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "* **L0 Codecs (`statcraft_io`):** Streaming CSV/TSV parser with automatic delimiter detection (`,`, `;`, `\\t`) and type inference (Numeric, Text, Date).\n* **L1 Data Engine (`statcraft_core`):** Tabular `DataSet`, `VariableDictionary` with measurement scales (`Scale`, `Ordinal`, `Nominal`), `ValueLabels`, `MissingValues`, and `DeltaBuffer` for granular cell Undo/Redo.\n* **L5 Command Bus (`statcraft_syntax`):** Typed `CommandBus` with readiness predicates (`enabled`) and JSON parameter specifications for AI agents.\n* **L6 Desktop GUI (`statcraft_app`):** `egui_dock` layout with 3 core workspaces (Data View, Variable View, Output Viewer).\n* **Localization (`statcraft_i18n`):** Fluent engine, `t!()` macro, and `i18n_lint_test` enforcing 0% raw Cyrillic strings in UI code.\n* **Branding & Windows Integration:** Vector icon embedded into PE executable resource `.rsrc` and window header."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793974413995837100",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "[x] Phase 2: L2 Mathematical Engine & Descriptive Statistics"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1793974413995837700",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "* **L2 Mathematical Algorithms (`statcraft_algo`):** `compute_descriptives` verified against Python `scipy.stats` reference values ($\\le 10^{-6}$ precision).\n* **L5 Command `DescriptivesCommand`:** Registered in `CommandBus`, emitting SPSS `DESCRIPTIVES VARIABLES=...` syntax.\n* **L6 Variable Picker Dialog:** Centered compact modal ($500 \\times 420$ px) with vector transfer chevrons and double-click support.\n* **L6 SPSS Pivot Table Display:** Full dock height in **Output Viewer** in authentic SPSS styling."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793974413995838600",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "[x] Phase 3: Frequency Analysis & Variable Dictionary Modals"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1793974413995839000",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "* **L2 `statcraft_algo`:** `compute_frequencies_detailed` procedure with value labels, missing value filtering, percentiles, and quartiles ($Q_1, Q_2, Q_3$).\n* **L5 Metadata Commands:** `var.set_value_labels` and `var.set_missing_values` with Undo/Redo history.\n* **L6 Metadata Editors & Dialogs:**\n  * Centered frequency modal `FrequenciesDialog`;\n  * Modal `ValueLabelsDialog` (`[...]` button in Values column);\n  * Modal `MissingValuesDialog` (discrete codes and numeric range);\n  * Toolbar button `1/A` in Data View for toggling numeric codes to human-readable labels."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793974413995840500",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "[x] Phase 4: Full Two-Way Reactive Data & Variable Grid"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1793974413995841000",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "* **L1 SPSS Type Engine:** Support for all 9 SPSS canonical variable types (`Numeric`, `Comma`, `Dot`, `Scientific`, `Date`, `Dollar`, `CustomCurrency`, `String`, `RestrictedNumeric`).\n* **L1 Blank Dataset Mode:** Immediate session readiness (`DataSet::blank(40, 0)`) without needing to load an external file.\n* **L6 Variable View:** Inline borderless editing of names and labels, interactive `▲ / ▼` spinners for width and decimals, alignment and role selectors, ghost add-row `*`.\n* **L6 Data View:** Inline cell editing with `Enter` / `Tab` navigation, row pre-warming when editing bottom row, row context menus.\n* **L6 VariableTypeDialog:** Modal type configuration dialog with width, precision, date format, and currency prefix settings."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793974413995842100",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "[x] Phase 5: Output Viewer Architecture & i18n Layout Shield"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1793974413995842500",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "* **Hierarchical Document Model:** `OutputProcedure`, `OutputNotes`, `OutputItem`, `OutputItemKind`, infinite continuous vertical document scroll.\n* **Interactive Outline Tree:** Vector icons for document root, procedure folders, syntax log, notes, pivot tables, and warnings.\n* **Synchronized Navigation:** Outline tree selection smoothly scrolls the canvas (`ui.scroll_to_rect`) with accent focus outline (`Tokens::ACCENT`).\n* **TSV Export:** Clipboard copying of pivot tables and frequencies preserving spreadsheet column alignment for Excel and Google Sheets.\n* **i18n Layout Shield:**\n  * Dynamic column width measurement via `layout_no_wrap` with horizontal scrolling;\n  * Strict cell clipping (`with_clip_rect`), preventing text spillover across columns;\n  * Compact vector outline toolbar buttons ($24 \\times 22$ px): `paint_icon_trash`, `paint_icon_expand_all`, `paint_icon_collapse_all` with hover tooltips."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793974413995843700",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "---"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793974413995844300",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "4. Multi-Document Dock Workspace Architecture (Dockable Workspace)"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1793974413995844700",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "Evolution of the docking architecture to provide maximum workflow flexibility while eliminating accidental data or panel loss:"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793974413995845500",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "4.1. Permanent System Workspaces (Permanent Tabs)"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1793974413995846000",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "* **Close Protection (`closeable = false`):**\n  * Core dataset tabs (**Data View** and **Variable View**) are session foundations and have no close button `[x]`. Users cannot accidentally close their dataset views.\n* **Authentic SPSS Mode Switcher:**\n  * Status bar tab buttons `[ Data View | Variable View ]` anchored at the bottom of the data grid, providing familiar one-click view toggling."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793974413995846800",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "4.2. \"Window\" Menu & Layout Management"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1793974413995847300",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "* **\"Window\" Menu:**\n  * Listing of all active views and documents with checkmarks indicating visibility;\n  * Quick-reveal for hidden or collapsed panels.\n* **Reset Workspace Layout:**\n  * `Window > Reset Workspace Layout` command immediately restores the default layout (e.g. Data View on the left, Output Viewer on the right, or clean tabs) if a user rearranges panels inconveniently.\n* **Layout Presets:**\n  * Analysis Preset (Data View left, Output Viewer right);\n  * Classic SPSS Preset (maximized single-tab documents);\n  * Scripting Preset (Syntax Editor top, Data View bottom)."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793974413995848500",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "4.3. Dynamic Document Tabs (User Document Tabs)"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1793974413995849000",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "Opened via `File > New / Open...`, equipped with standard close buttons `[x]` and dirty-state confirmation prompts:\n1. **Multi-Dataset Management (`DataSet1`, `DataSet2`, ...):**\n   * Concurrent multi-file workflow in a single session;\n   * Split View for side-by-side comparison of datasets;\n   * Required foundation for file merger operations (*Merge Files: Add Cases / Add Variables*).\n2. **Syntax Editor (`.sps`):**\n   * Dedicated syntax script editor tab with line numbering, keyword syntax highlighting, and batch execution `Run`;\n   * Destination for the `Paste` button from analysis dialogs.\n3. **Multiple Output Documents (`.spv`):**\n   * Support for parallel output logs (e.g., exploratory scratchpad vs. clean publication report).\n4. **Interactive Chart Editor:**\n   * Visualization tabs featuring *Brushing & Linking* (selecting points or bars automatically highlights corresponding cases in Data View).\n5. **AI Copilot Console (StatCraft Copilot / `statcraft_bridge`):**\n   * Conversational terminal for executing analyses, data transformations, and natural language interpretation via Model Context Protocol (MCP)."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793974413995850500",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "4.4. \"File\" Menu Architecture, StatCraft Projects (.stc), and SPSS (.sav / .zsav) Codecs"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1793974413995851100",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "Upgrading the File menu from a primitive CSV loader into an all-inclusive research lifecycle management hub:"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793974413995851700",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "#### A. Unified Workspace Project Container (`.stc` — StatCraft Project)\nIn classic SPSS, datasets (`.sav`), output logs (`.spv`), and scripts (`.sps`) are fragmented across disconnected files, often severing the link between reports and specific data versions.\n* **The `.stc` Project Format:** A native, open format built on Apache Parquet and structured JSON metadata, packaging into a single hermetic container:\n  1. The complete tabular dataset (`DataSet`);\n  2. The full variable dictionary with rich metadata (`VariableDictionary`: types, measurement scales, `ValueLabels`, user and system missing values `MissingValues`, alignment, column widths, decimal precision);\n  3. The entire `Output Viewer` workbook (all generated procedures, pivot tables, frequency distributions, `Notes` blocks, and syntax execution history);\n  4. Application UI layout state and docking topology (`DockState`), restoring the user's workspace exactly as it was when reopened."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793974413995853400",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "#### B. Native Support for IBM SPSS Statistics Formats (`.sav` and `.zsav`)\nDirect opening of SPSS data files without converters or proprietary closed-source libraries (Clean-Room canon on L0 `statcraft_io`):\n* Binary `.sav` reading conforming to the open GNU PSPP specification;\n* Streaming decompression of compressed `.zsav` archives using zlib;\n* Automatic conversion of SPSS variable records into the internal `VariableDictionary` (measurement levels, `SYSMIS` codes, multibyte character encodings);\n* Export back to `.sav` for seamless round-trip compatibility with SPSS users."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793974413995854400",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "#### C. Hierarchical Structure of the \"File\" Menu\n* **New ▶:**\n  * New Project (`.stc`) — `Ctrl+Shift+N`;\n  * New Dataset (Blank Sheet) — `Ctrl+N`;\n  * Syntax File (`.sps`).\n* **Open Project (`.stc`)...** — `Ctrl+Shift+O`.\n* **Open Data (`.sav`, `.zsav`, `.csv`, `.tsv`, `.stc`)...** — `Ctrl+O`.\n* **Import Data ▶:**\n  * SPSS Data File (`*.sav`, `*.zsav`)...\n  * Delimited Text File (CSV, TSV, TXT)...\n  * Excel Spreadsheet (`*.xlsx`)... (future roadmap).\n* **Recent Projects & Files ▶:** Fast launch for the last 10 session files with on-disk path history.\n* **Save Project (`.stc`)** — `Ctrl+S`.\n* **Save Project As...** — `Ctrl+Shift+S`.\n* **Save Data As (`.sav`, `.csv`, `.tsv`)...**\n* **Export ▶:**\n  * Export Output Workbook (HTML, PDF, TSV)...\n  * Export Dataset to CSV / Excel...\n* **Close Project** — `Ctrl+W`.\n* **Exit** — `Alt+F4`."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793974413995856200",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "4.5. \"Edit\" Menu Architecture"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1793974413995856800",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "The central operational hub for data manipulation, bidirectional command history, and dataset navigation:\n* **Bidirectional History Stack:**\n  * Full Undo/Redo (`Ctrl+Z`, `Ctrl+Y` / `Ctrl+Shift+Z`) backed by `CommandBus` for all data grid, variable dictionary, and analysis steps.\n* **Specialized Clipboard Operations:**\n  * Cut (`Ctrl+X`), Copy (`Ctrl+C`), Paste (`Ctrl+V`), Clear (`Delete`);\n  * **Copy with Variable Names (`Ctrl+Shift+C`):** exports selected cells with an auto-generated header row, ready for pasting into external spreadsheets and publication reports.\n* **High-Capacity Dataset Navigation:**\n  * **Go to Case (`Ctrl+G`):** instant virtualized scrolling jump to a case by line number (essential for datasets with hundreds of thousands or millions of cases);\n  * **Go to Variable (`Ctrl+J`):** fuzzy search and column focus by variable name or descriptive label across large questionnaires.\n* **Grid Search and Replacement:**\n  * Find (`Ctrl+F`): substring or exact case-sensitive matching across columns;\n  * Replace (`Ctrl+H`): batch category code and typo replacement.\n* **Insert Case & Insert Variable:** Insert a new row or column immediately before the active cursor position.\n* **Options / Preferences Dialog:** Modular environment configuration dialog:\n  * *Tab 1: General:* UI language (EN/RU), visual theme, recent files limit, session auto-save interval;\n  * *Tab 2: Data Grid:* decimal separator selection (dot `12.5` vs. comma `12,5`), new variable defaults (width 8, decimals 2), show value labels by default;\n  * *Tab 3: Fonts & Scale:* table grid font size (9–14 pt), UI scaling factor (100%, 125%, 150% for HiDPI/4K);\n  * *Tab 4: Output:* pivot table visual style (Classic SPSS, Academic APA), $p$-value styling (`* p < .05`, `** p < .01`);\n  * *Tab 5: AI & MCP Bridge:* MCP server socket port (18492), dataset access permissions, interpretation verbosity."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793974413995858800",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "4.6. \"View\" Menu Architecture"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1793974413995859500",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "Managing data presentation, visual readability, language switching, and color themes:\n* **UI Language ▶:** Runtime language switching without restart (`Russian`, `English`, effortlessly extensible by dropping new `.ftl` files into `locales/`).\n* **Value Labels — `1/A`:** Instant toggling between raw numeric codes and human-readable descriptive category labels (`1` $\\leftrightarrow$ `Male`).\n* **Visual Themes ▶:**\n  * **Light Theme (Classic SPSS):** traditional light grey/white background with contrast grid lines and blue header accents familiar to SPSS users;\n  * **Dark Theme (Dark Pro):** modern dark aesthetic engineered to minimize eye strain during long-session analysis;\n  * **Auto (System):** automatic synchronization with the host Windows OS dark/light mode preference.\n* **Zoom & Font Size:**\n  * Rapid table font scaling (`Ctrl++`, `Ctrl+-`, `Ctrl+0`);\n  * Tailored readability on high-DPI (4K/Retina) displays.\n* **Grid Lines:** Toggle cell border rendering visibility on the data canvas.\n* **Status Bar:**\n  * Displays case count $N$, variable count $P$, and memory footprint;\n  * Live status flags: active selection filter (`Filter On`), sample weighting (`Weight On`), and file split (`Split File On`).\n* **Toolbars:** Show/hide the top vector action toolbar."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793974413995861000",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "4.7. \"Data\" Menu Architecture"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1793974413995861700",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "Matrix-level data manipulation, dataset topology, and sample conditioning:\n* **Sort Cases...:** Multi-level ascending/descending observation sorting across one or multiple variables;\n* **Sort Variables...:** Reorder columns in data and variable dictionary views by name, type, label, or measurement level;\n* **Transpose...:** Matrix rotation swapping rows into columns and columns into rows;\n* **Merge Files ▶:**\n  * **Add Cases...:** vertical dataset concatenation (combining waves of observations);\n  * **Add Variables...:** horizontal relational table joining by primary key ID (JOIN / VLOOKUP);\n* **Restructure...:** Format transformation between Wide (repeated measurements in distinct columns) and Long (time factor and score column) required for repeated-measures ANOVA and mixed models;\n* **Aggregate...:** Collapsing observation rows with group-level summaries (means, sums, medians);\n* **Split File...:** Global mode executing all analytical procedures separately per subgroup with live `[Split File On]` status bar flag;\n* **Select Cases...:** Filtering cases by logical criteria (`Age >= 18 AND Income > 0`) with strikethrough visual masking and `[Filter On]` status bar flag;\n* **Weight Cases...:** Applying sampling weights to balance representative population margins with `[Weight On]` status bar flag."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793974413995864000",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "4.8. \"Transform\" Menu Architecture — 100% Parity with IBM SPSS Statistics"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1793974413995865000",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "The comprehensive mathematical feature engineering, data imputation, and matrix conditioning toolchain:\n* **Compute Variable...:** Column formula calculator supporting arithmetic (`SQRT`, `ABS`, `LN`, `EXP`), row-wise statistics (`MEAN`, `SUM`, `SD`, `MIN`, `MAX`), string functions (`CONCAT`, `SUBSTR`), and conditional logical assignments (`IF (condition) Target = expression`);\n* **Shift Values (Lead & Lag)...:** Time-series lag/lead operators (`LAG(x, 1)`) for autoregressive econometric modeling and rate-of-change calculation;\n* **Recode ▶:**\n  * **Recode into Different Variables...:** Non-destructive continuous-to-categorical binning (e.g. age cohorts, income brackets) into a newly minted variable;\n  * **Recode into Same Variables...:** In-place modification of existing column cells;\n  * **Automatic Recode...:** Instant alphanumeric text conversion into contiguous integer codes (`1`, `2`) accompanied by automatic generation of dictionary `ValueLabels`;\n* **Create Dummy Variables...:** Instant transformation of multi-category discrete scales into binary 0/1 indicator columns for multiple regression models;\n* **Visual Binning...:** Interactive modal featuring a live histogram preview with draggable cut points for slicing variables into equal percentiles, cut points, or standard deviation intervals;\n* **Optimal Binning...:** Supervised discretization optimizing predictor bin relationships against a categorical target variable;\n* **Prepare Data for Modeling (ADP)...:** Automated data preparation, anomaly screening, and statistical normalization;\n* **Rank Cases...:** Order rank calculation with tie handling (Mean, Low, High ties);\n* **Date and Time Wizard...:** Multi-step wizard for date arithmetic: duration calculation (exact age, tenure), date addition/subtraction, component extraction (day of week, quarter, year);\n* **Create Time Series...:** Moving averages, exponential smoothing series, and difference transforms to eliminate secular trend;\n* **Replace Missing Values (Data Imputation)...:** Algorithmic gap filling via Series Mean, Mean of Nearby Points, Median of Nearby Points, Linear Interpolation, or Linear Trend at point;\n* **Random Number Generators & Seed...:** Pseudorandom seed initialization guaranteeing 100% reproducibility in split-sample validation and Monte Carlo experiments;\n* **Count Values within Cases...:** Row-wise targeted value occurrence counter (survey battery scales, symptom clusters);\n* **Programmability Transformations...:** Custom execution of transformation pipelines via the local `statcraft_bridge` socket."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793974413995867200",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "4.9. \"Analyze\" Menu Architecture — 100% Parity with IBM SPSS Statistics"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1793974413995868000",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "The complete inventory of applied statistical procedures organized by canonical thematic submenus:\n* **Descriptive Statistics ▶:**\n  * **Frequencies...:** frequency distributions, percentages, valid percentages, cumulative percentages, custom percentiles, quartiles ($Q_1, Q_2, Q_3$);\n  * **Descriptives...:** mean, standard error, variance, standard deviation, minimum, maximum, range, skewness $G_1$, kurtosis $G_2$;\n  * **Explore...:** exploratory data analysis (EDA), Boxplots, stem-and-leaf plots, Kolmogorov-Smirnov (with Lilliefors significance correction) and Shapiro-Wilk normality tests;\n  * **Crosstabs...:** two-way contingency tables, Pearson Chi-Square ($\\chi^2$), Fisher's Exact Test, Yates' continuity correction, association coefficients (Cramér's $V$, $\\phi$, contingency coefficient);\n* **Compare Means ▶:**\n  * **One-Sample T Test...:** test sample mean against an external hypothesized parameter $\\mu_0$;\n  * **Independent-Samples T Test...:** two-group mean difference testing, Levene's test for equality of variances (reporting Student's $t$ and Welch's $t$);\n  * **Paired-Samples T Test...:** dependent matched-pairs / repeated-measures \"before-and-after\" testing;\n  * **One-Way ANOVA...:** between-group and within-group variance analysis for $3+$ groups with post-hoc multiple comparisons (Tukey HSD, Bonferroni correction);\n* **General Linear Model (GLM) ▶:**\n  * **Univariate (ANCOVA)...:** analysis of covariance conditioning on continuous metric covariates;\n  * **Multivariate (MANOVA)...:** multivariate analysis of variance evaluating multiple continuous dependent variables simultaneously;\n  * **Repeated Measures ANOVA...:** longitudinal experimental designs with Mauchly's test of sphericity;\n* **Correlate ▶:**\n  * **Bivariate...:** Pearson product-moment ($r$), Spearman rank-order ($\\rho$), and Kendall tau ($\\tau$) correlation matrices with two-tailed significance testing;\n  * **Partial...:** linear association between two variables controlling for the linear effect of one or more additional covariates;\n* **Regression ▶:**\n  * **Linear...:** multiple Ordinary Least Squares (OLS) regression, unstandardized $B$ and standardized $\\beta$ coefficients, $R^2$, ANOVA $F$-test, collinearity diagnostics (VIF, Tolerance);\n  * **Binary Logistic...:** dichotomous event probability modeling (0/1), Odds Ratios $\\text{Exp}(B)$, Wald test, Hosmer-Lemeshow goodness-of-fit;\n  * **Multinomial & Ordinal Logistic...:** multi-category unordered and ordered logit modeling;\n  * **Curve Estimation...:** quadratic, cubic, logarithmic, inverse, and power curve fitting;\n* **Nonparametric Tests ▶:**\n  * **Independent Samples:** Mann-Whitney $U$ test (2 groups), Kruskal-Wallis $H$ test ($K$ groups);\n  * **Related Samples:** Wilcoxon signed-rank test (2 paired conditions), Friedman test ($K$ conditions);\n* **Dimension Reduction & Classify ▶:**\n  * **Factor Analysis / PCA...:** sampling adequacy (KMO, Bartlett's sphericity test), Scree plot eigenvalue extraction, Varimax orthogonal rotation;\n  * **Cluster Analysis...:** $K$-Means clustering and agglomerative hierarchical clustering with proximity distance matrices and dendrogram visualization;\n* **Scale > Reliability Analysis...:** Internal consistency evaluation via Cronbach's Alpha ($\\alpha$) and item-deleted scale sensitivity statistics;\n* **Survival ▶:** Actuarial Life Tables, Kaplan-Meier product-limit survivor curves with Log-Rank tests, Cox Proportional Hazards Regression."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793974413995871300",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "4.10. \"Direct Marketing\" Menu Architecture — Commercial Extension"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1793974413995872100",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "Applied decision-support and customer segmentation toolchain for CRM and commercial marketing analytics (*slated for late-stage implementation following completion of core statistical procedures*):\n* **RFM Analysis (Recency, Frequency, Monetary)...:** Customer transactional scoring partitioning client databases into actionable tiers (Champions, Loyal, Promising, At Risk, Dormant);\n* **Profile Potential Contacts...:** Comparative demographic and behavioral profiling identifying characteristics of positive campaign respondents;\n* **Cluster Analysis for Segmentation...:** Simplified customer clustering wizard tailored for domain marketing practitioners;\n* **Control Package Test (A/B Testing)...:** Statistical testing verifying significant response rate improvements across campaign variants;\n* **Postal Code Response Rate...:** Geographic segmentation evaluating localized conversion efficiency across regions."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793974413995873200",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "4.11. \"Graphs\" Menu Architecture — L3 statcraft_charts Vector Engine"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1793974413995873800",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "Interactive scientific visualization engine built on `egui_plot` featuring bidirectional data canvas coupling (Brushing & Linking) and publication-grade vector export:\n* **Chart Builder...:** Interactive visual canvas featuring a drag-and-drop gallery of graph elements onto coordinate axes ($X$, $Y$) and cluster grouping slots;\n* **Histogram...:** Continuous distribution plotting with configurable binning intervals and theoretical Gaussian normal curve overlay;\n* **Bar Chart...:** Simple, clustered, and stacked bar diagrams with 95% confidence interval error bars;\n* **Boxplot («Box-and-Whisker»)...:** Visualization of medians, interquartile ranges ($IQR$), $1.5 \\times IQR$ fences, and labeled outlier observation markers;\n* **Scatter / Dot Plot...:** Bivariate point clouds with linear regression trendlines and $N \\times N$ scatterplot matrices for correlation screening;\n* **Error Bar...:** Mean comparisons displaying confidence intervals and standard errors;\n* **Pie Chart...:** Category share proportions with percentage badges;\n* **Line Chart...:** Longitudinal trajectory and time series trend tracking;\n* **Population Pyramid...:** Bilateral demographic distribution plots;\n* **Brushing & Linking Interactivity:** Selecting points or bars on the plot dynamically highlights corresponding records in Data View;\n* **Vector Graphics Export:** True vector SVG export (ideal for peer-reviewed academic journals without resolution degradation) and high-DPI raster PNG (300+ DPI)."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793974413995875200",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "4.12. \"Utilities\" Menu Architecture — Metadata & Questionnaire Structure"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1793974413995875700",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "Dictionary inspection, large-scale questionnaire partitioning, and dataset documentation:\n* **Variables / Quick Inspector...:** Floating rapid-inspection modal displaying complete metadata for any variable (data type, survey question label, `ValueLabels` table, missing value rules) with a direct cursor focus jump in the active grid without switching tabs;\n* **Variable Sets (Define & Use)...:** Logical grouping of hundreds of questionnaire items into named domain subsets (\"Demographics\", \"Depression Scales\", \"Financial History\") to filter variable picker lists across all analysis dialogs;\n* **Data File Comments...:** Embedded research annotation log tracking audit history, cleaning steps, and sample origins stored directly within `.stc` and `.sav` headers;\n* **Codebook Generator...:** Automatic compilation of a comprehensive study codebook tabulating all dictionary scales, category encodings, and value distributions for documentation and archival handoff."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793974413995876900",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "4.13. \"Extensions\" Menu Architecture — Extensibility, AI MCP & Scripting"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1793974413995877400",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "The open scientific ecosystem bridge integrating external community packages, custom interfaces, and agentic AI models:\n* **Extension Hub...:** Centralized repository browsing, discovering, and installing community-authored procedure packages with one-click installation;\n* **Install Local Extension (.scpl)...:** Offline package installer for StatCraft Plugin archives (`.scpl`) adhering to the *Zero-Core Hardcoding* canon;\n* **Custom Dialog Builder...:** Graphical form designer enabling analysts without low-level Rust experience to construct bespoke dialog modals rendered natively on `egui` and mapped to syntax/Python pipelines;\n* **AI & Model Context Protocol (MCP) Hub...:** Operational console monitoring the internal MCP server, exposing tools for autonomous orchestration by external AI agents (Antigravity, Claude, local LLMs);\n* **Scripting Runtime Bridge (Python & R Bridge via `statcraft_bridge`)...:** IPC socket management (18492) and runtime environment path binding for executing custom statistical scripts with safe Arrow memory sharing."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793974413995878500",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "4.14. \"Window\" Menu Architecture — Docking Management & Layout Presets"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1793974413995879000",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "Orchestration of the `egui_dock` multi-document interface, layout safeguards, and split-screen workflows:\n* **Reset Workspace Layout...:** Panic recovery command restoring default factory topology (Data View on the left, Output Viewer on the right) when panels are accidentally closed or misaligned;\n* **Layout Presets ▶:**\n  * *Analysis Preset (Split View):* simultaneous view of the data matrix on the left and live calculation reports on the right;\n  * *Classic SPSS Preset:* maximized document tabs spanning the entire window frame;\n  * *Scripting Preset:* horizontal split with Syntax Editor `.sps` on top and Data View below;\n* **Active Document & View Listing (with direct shortcuts and visibility checks):**\n  * `[✓] Data View` — `Ctrl+1`;\n  * `[✓] Variable View` — `Ctrl+2`;\n  * `[✓] Output Viewer` — `Ctrl+3`;\n  * `[ ] Syntax Editor` — `Ctrl+4`;\n  * `[ ] AI Copilot Console` — `Ctrl+5`;\n* **Minimize All / Restore All Panels.**"
      },
