    },
    {
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "5. Analytical Roadmap Ahead"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1793974413995884500",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "[x] Phase 6: Compare Means & Hypothesis Testing"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1793974413995885000",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "* **One-Sample T-Test:**\n  * Compares sample mean against hypothesized test value $\\mu_0$;\n  * $t$-statistic, degrees of freedom $df$, two-tailed $p$-value, 95% confidence interval of the difference.\n* **Independent-Samples T-Test:**\n  * Levene's Test for Equality of Variances ($F$-statistic and $p$-value);\n  * Student's $t$-test (equal variances assumed) and Welch's $t$-test (equal variances not assumed);\n  * Grouping variable and group definition dialog.\n* **Paired-Samples T-Test:**\n  * Repeated measures / paired observations, pair correlation, difference $t$-statistic.\n* **One-Way ANOVA:**\n  * Between-group and within-group Sum of Squares ($SS$), Mean Squares ($MS$), Fisher's $F$-test;\n  * Post-Hoc Tests: Tukey HSD, Bonferroni correction."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793974413995886400",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "[ ] Phase 7: Association Analysis & Non-Parametric Tests"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1793974413995886900",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "* **Crosstabulations (Crosstabs):**\n  * Two-way contingency tables for nominal/ordinal scales;\n  * Observed and expected counts, row/column/total percentages;\n  * Pearson Chi-Square ($\\chi^2$), Yates' continuity correction, Fisher's Exact Test ($2 \\times 2$);\n  * Directional and symmetric measures: Pearson contingency coefficient, Cramér's $V$, $\\phi$.\n* **Bivariate Correlations:**\n  * Pearson linear correlation ($r$);\n  * Spearman ($\\rho$) and Kendall ($\\tau$) rank correlations;\n  * Correlation matrix with significance stars ($* p < 0.05$, $** p < 0.01$).\n* **Non-Parametric Tests:**\n  * Mann-Whitney $U$ test (independent two-group alternative);\n  * Wilcoxon signed-rank test (paired samples alternative);\n  * Kruskal-Wallis $H$ test (one-way ANOVA alternative)."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793974413995888200",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "[ ] Phase 8: Data Manipulation & Transformation"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1793974413995888700",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "* **Compute Variable:**\n  * Built-in safe expression parser (`TARGET = VAR_A + SQRT(VAR_B)`);\n  * Mathematical, statistical, and conditional functions (`SUM`, `MEAN`, `ABS`, `LN`, `EXP`, `IF`);\n  * Calculator dialog with function palette and variable selector.\n* **Recode:**\n  * «Recode into Same Variables» and «Recode into Different Variables»;\n  * Range mapping interface (`1 thru 18 -> 1`, `19 thru 65 -> 2`, `ELSE -> Copy`).\n* **Data Management:**\n  * Sort Cases by multiple keys (ascending/descending);\n  * Select Cases (filtering observations by logical condition);\n  * Merge Files (add cases or add variables by key)."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793974413995890200",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "[ ] Phase 9: Statistical Graphics & Visualization"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1793974413995890700",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "* **Vector Plotting Engine (`egui_plot`):**\n  * **Histogram:** configurable bin widths, superimposed normal curve;\n  * **Bar Chart:** simple, clustered, stacked bars with 95% error bars;\n  * **Boxplot:** median, IQR box, 1.5 IQR whiskers, outlier markers;\n  * **Scatter Plot:** 2D point cloud with linear regression fit line;\n  * **Pie Chart:** categorical share breakdown.\n* **Brushing & Linking:**\n  * Selecting data points in a chart automatically highlights corresponding rows in Data View.\n* **High-Resolution Vector Export:** SVG and PNG export."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793974413995891800",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "[ ] Phase 10: Regression & Multivariate Analytics"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1793974413995892300",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "* **Linear Regression:**\n  * Ordinary Least Squares (OLS);\n  * Coefficients ($B$, $SE_B$, standardized $\\beta$, $t$-statistic, $p$-value);\n  * Model summary: $R$, $R^2$, adjusted $R^2$, ANOVA $F$;\n  * Multicollinearity diagnostics (VIF, Tolerance).\n* **Binary Logistic Regression:**\n  * Maximum likelihood estimation;\n  * Odds Ratios ($\\text{Exp}(B)$), Wald test, pseudo-$R^2$ (Cox & Snell, Nagelkerke).\n* **Principal Component Analysis (PCA / Factor Analysis):**\n  * KMO sample adequacy and Bartlett's test of sphericity;\n  * Eigenvalue extraction ($\\lambda > 1$) and scree plot;\n  * Varimax orthogonal rotation.\n* **Reliability Analysis:**\n  * Cronbach's Alpha ($\\alpha$) for scale internal consistency;\n  * Item-total statistics (alpha if item deleted).\n* **Cluster Analysis:**\n  * $K$-Means clustering;\n  * Hierarchical clustering with dendrogram."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793974413995893900",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "[ ] Phase 11: File Codecs & Reporting"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1793974413995894500",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "* **IBM SPSS `.sav` and `.zsav` Codec:**\n  * Native clean-room read/write support without proprietary DLLs;\n  * Full preservation of metadata: variable labels, value labels, measure scales, missing values (`SYSMIS`);\n  * Support for compressed `.zsav`.\n* **StatCraft Native Project Codec `.stc`:**\n  * High-performance columnar storage based on Apache Parquet and JSON metadata.\n* **Document Export:**\n  * Export Output Viewer books into PDF, Word DOCX, LaTeX, HTML, and Excel (`.xlsx`)."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793974413995895600",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "[ ] Phase 12: Syntax Engine & AI Ecosystem"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1793974413995896100",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "* **Interactive Syntax Editor:**\n  * Dedicated script workspace for SPSS syntax (`.sps`);\n  * Syntax highlighting, line numbers, autocomplete;\n  * `Paste` button in all dialogs emits syntax directly into editor.\n* **Built-in Model Context Protocol (MCP) Server:**\n  * Connect external AI agents (Antigravity, Claude, local LLMs) directly to running StatCraft;\n  * MCP tools: inspect dictionary, execute analyses, stream natural language interpretations directly into Output Viewer.\n* **StatCraft CLI:**\n  * Headless runner for automated batch pipelines: `statcraft-cli --run script.sps --output report.html`."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793974413995897300",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "[ ] Phase 13: Advanced & Specialty Modules"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1793974413995897800",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "* **Survival Analysis (Biostatistics & Medical Science):**\n  * Life Tables analysis;\n  * Kaplan-Meier estimation with Log-Rank, Breslow, and Tarone-Ware tests;\n  * Cox Proportional Hazards Regression with time-dependent covariates.\n* **Time Series & Forecasting:**\n  * Autoregressive Integrated Moving Average (*ARIMA / SARIMA*);\n  * Exponential Smoothing (Single, Holt linear, Winters seasonal);\n  * Autocorrelation and Partial Autocorrelation Functions (ACF / PACF);\n  * Unit root / Stationarity tests (Augmented Dickey-Fuller ADF).\n* **Generalized Linear Models (GLM / GENLIN):**\n  * Poisson Regression for count and rare event data;\n  * Negative Binomial Regression for overdispersed count data;\n  * Gamma Regression and Inverse Gaussian models.\n* **Linear Mixed Models (LMM):**\n  * Hierarchical Linear Models (HLM) for multi-level data;\n  * Repeated Measures ANOVA with random intercepts and slopes;\n  * Flexible residual covariance structures (Auto-regressive AR(1), Compound Symmetry, Unstructured).\n* **Complex Samples Analysis:**\n  * Multi-stage stratified and clustered sample survey analysis;\n  * Sampling weight adjustments with Taylor series variance estimation.\n* **Specialized Marketing & Social Research Procedures:**\n  * Multidimensional Scaling (*PROXSCAL / ALSCAL*);\n  * Simple and Multiple Correspondence Analysis;\n  * Conjoint Analysis;\n  * Decision & Classification Trees (*CHAID, Exhaustive CHAID, CRT, QUEST*)."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793974413995900100",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "---"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793974413995902500",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "5. Quality Assurance & Definition of Done"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1793974413995903000",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "Every roadmap feature is committed strictly when satisfying:\n1. **Resource Guard:** `-j 1` on all cargo commands.\n2. **100% Test Pass:** 0 failures, Golden Oracle precision $\\le 10^{-6}$.\n3. **i18n Linter:** 0 hardcoded strings in UI.\n4. **Layer Integrity:** `cargo xtask layers` passes.\n5. **Clean Linters:** `cargo clippy --workspace -j 1 -- -D warnings` and `cargo fmt --check`.\n6. **Bilingual Chronicle:** Synchronous entries in `docs/CHRONICLE.md` and `docs/CHRONICLE.en.md`."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1793974413995904100",
