<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="generator" content="CapsuleCraft Native"></head><body style="font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,sans-serif;max-width:720px;margin:32px auto;line-height:1.55;color:#23201c;background:#faf8f4;"><h1>📚 StatCraft / StatCraft — Strategic Roadmap</h1><p><em>[callout block — open in CapsuleCraft web for its canvas]</em></p><h1>StatCraft — Strategic Roadmap</h1><h3>High-Performance Open-Source Statistical Package in 100% Pure Safe Rust</h3><p>**ArtCraft (`storytold`) Ecosystem Canon | Dual-licensed under MIT OR Apache-2.0**</p><p>---</p><h2>1. Mission and Architectural Canon</h2><p>**StatCraft** is built as an uncompromising, high-performance, crash-proof, and fully open alternative to IBM SPSS Statistics.</p><p>* **100% Safe Rust &amp; Never Crash:** Zero `unsafe`, zero `panic!`, zero `unwrap()`. Malformed input, empty arrays, or division by zero will never crash the application.<br>* **Commands, Not Handlers:** Every user action and analytical procedure is an engine command (`EngineCommand`) supporting Undo/Redo, serialization into classic SPSS syntax (`.sps`), and automation by AI agents.<br>* **Agent-First Architecture:** Built-in Model Context Protocol (MCP) and local IPC socket for native external AI orchestrator control and automated natural language interpretations in Output Viewer.<br>* **Zero-Hardcode i18n:** 100% UI string isolation in Fluent catalogs (`ru.ftl`, `en.ftl`) with runtime language switching without restarting.<br>* **Vector-First UI:** Clean vector rendering for widgets, scale indicators, and badges via `ui.painter()` and cached SVGs. Strict prohibition of emoji and rare Unicode characters that cause &quot;tofu&quot; boxes (`□`).<br>* **Resource Guard:** Compilation and testing strictly throttled (`jobs = 1`, `codegen-units = 1`) to preserve user workstation stability.</p><p>---</p><h2>2. Development Status Matrix</h2><p><em>[code block — open in CapsuleCraft web for its canvas]</em></p><p>---</p><h2>3. Delivered Milestones</h2><h3>[x] Phase 1: Scaffolding, Core MVP &amp; UI Foundation</h3><p>* **L0 Codecs (`statcraft_io`):** Streaming CSV/TSV parser with automatic delimiter detection (`,`, `;`, `\t`) and type inference (Numeric, Text, Date).<br>* **L1 Data Engine (`statcraft_core`):** Tabular `DataSet`, `VariableDictionary` with measurement scales (`Scale`, `Ordinal`, `Nominal`), `ValueLabels`, `MissingValues`, and `DeltaBuffer` for granular cell Undo/Redo.<br>* **L5 Command Bus (`statcraft_syntax`):** Typed `CommandBus` with readiness predicates (`enabled`) and JSON parameter specifications for AI agents.<br>* **L6 Desktop GUI (`statcraft_app`):** `egui_dock` layout with 3 core workspaces (Data View, Variable View, Output Viewer).<br>* **Localization (`statcraft_i18n`):** Fluent engine, `t!()` macro, and `i18n_lint_test` enforcing 0% raw Cyrillic strings in UI code.<br>* **Branding &amp; Windows Integration:** Vector icon embedded into PE executable resource `.rsrc` and window header.</p><h3>[x] Phase 2: L2 Mathematical Engine &amp; Descriptive Statistics</h3><p>* **L2 Mathematical Algorithms (`statcraft_algo`):** `compute_descriptives` verified against Python `scipy.stats` reference values ($\le 10^{-6}$ precision).<br>* **L5 Command `DescriptivesCommand`:** Registered in `CommandBus`, emitting SPSS `DESCRIPTIVES VARIABLES=...` syntax.<br>* **L6 Variable Picker Dialog:** Centered compact modal ($500 \times 420$ px) with vector transfer chevrons and double-click support.<br>* **L6 SPSS Pivot Table Display:** Full dock height in **Output Viewer** in authentic SPSS styling.</p><h3>[x] Phase 3: Frequency Analysis &amp; Variable Dictionary Modals</h3><p>* **L2 `statcraft_algo`:** `compute_frequencies_detailed` procedure with value labels, missing value filtering, percentiles, and quartiles ($Q_1, Q_2, Q_3$).<br>* **L5 Metadata Commands:** `var.set_value_labels` and `var.set_missing_values` with Undo/Redo history.<br>* **L6 Metadata Editors &amp; Dialogs:**<br>  * Centered frequency modal `FrequenciesDialog`;<br>  * Modal `ValueLabelsDialog` (`[...]` button in Values column);<br>  * Modal `MissingValuesDialog` (discrete codes and numeric range);<br>  * Toolbar button `1/A` in Data View for toggling numeric codes to human-readable labels.</p><h3>[x] Phase 4: Full Two-Way Reactive Data &amp; Variable Grid</h3><p>* **L1 SPSS Type Engine:** Support for all 9 SPSS canonical variable types (`Numeric`, `Comma`, `Dot`, `Scientific`, `Date`, `Dollar`, `CustomCurrency`, `String`, `RestrictedNumeric`).<br>* **L1 Blank Dataset Mode:** Immediate session readiness (`DataSet::blank(40, 0)`) without needing to load an external file.<br>* **L6 Variable View:** Inline borderless editing of names and labels, interactive `▲ / ▼` spinners for width and decimals, alignment and role selectors, ghost add-row `*`.<br>* **L6 Data View:** Inline cell editing with `Enter` / `Tab` navigation, row pre-warming when editing bottom row, row context menus.<br>* **L6 VariableTypeDialog:** Modal type configuration dialog with width, precision, date format, and currency prefix settings.</p><h3>[x] Phase 5: Output Viewer Architecture &amp; i18n Layout Shield</h3><p>* **Hierarchical Document Model:** `OutputProcedure`, `OutputNotes`, `OutputItem`, `OutputItemKind`, infinite continuous vertical document scroll.<br>* **Interactive Outline Tree:** Vector icons for document root, procedure folders, syntax log, notes, pivot tables, and warnings.<br>* **Synchronized Navigation:** Outline tree selection smoothly scrolls the canvas (`ui.scroll_to_rect`) with accent focus outline (`Tokens::ACCENT`).<br>* **TSV Export:** Clipboard copying of pivot tables and frequencies preserving spreadsheet column alignment for Excel and Google Sheets.<br>* **i18n Layout Shield:**<br>  * Dynamic column width measurement via `layout_no_wrap` with horizontal scrolling;<br>  * Strict cell clipping (`with_clip_rect`), preventing text spillover across columns;<br>  * Compact vector outline toolbar buttons ($24 \times 22$ px): `paint_icon_trash`, `paint_icon_expand_all`, `paint_icon_collapse_all` with hover tooltips.</p><p>---</p><h2>4. Multi-Document Dock Workspace Architecture (Dockable Workspace)</h2><p>Evolution of the docking architecture to provide maximum workflow flexibility while eliminating accidental data or panel loss:</p><h3>4.1. Permanent System Workspaces (Permanent Tabs)</h3><p>* **Close Protection (`closeable = false`):**<br>  * Core dataset tabs (**Data View** and **Variable View**) are session foundations and have no close button `[x]`. Users cannot accidentally close their dataset views.<br>* **Authentic SPSS Mode Switcher:**<br>  * Status bar tab buttons `[ Data View | Variable View ]` anchored at the bottom of the data grid, providing familiar one-click view toggling.</p><h3>4.2. &quot;Window&quot; Menu &amp; Layout Management</h3><p>* **&quot;Window&quot; Menu:**<br>  * Listing of all active views and documents with checkmarks indicating visibility;<br>  * Quick-reveal for hidden or collapsed panels.<br>* **Reset Workspace Layout:**<br>  * `Window &gt; Reset Workspace Layout` command immediately restores the default layout (e.g. Data View on the left, Output Viewer on the right, or clean tabs) if a user rearranges panels inconveniently.<br>* **Layout Presets:**<br>  * Analysis Preset (Data View left, Output Viewer right);<br>  * Classic SPSS Preset (maximized single-tab documents);<br>  * Scripting Preset (Syntax Editor top, Data View bottom).</p><h3>4.3. Dynamic Document Tabs (User Document Tabs)</h3><p>Opened via `File &gt; New / Open...`, equipped with standard close buttons `[x]` and dirty-state confirmation prompts:<br>1. **Multi-Dataset Management (`DataSet1`, `DataSet2`, ...):**<br>   * Concurrent multi-file workflow in a single session;<br>   * Split View for side-by-side comparison of datasets;<br>   * Required foundation for file merger operations (*Merge Files: Add Cases / Add Variables*).<br>2. **Syntax Editor (`.sps`):**<br>   * Dedicated syntax script editor tab with line numbering, keyword syntax highlighting, and batch execution `Run`;<br>   * Destination for the `Paste` button from analysis dialogs.<br>3. **Multiple Output Documents (`.spv`):**<br>   * Support for parallel output logs (e.g., exploratory scratchpad vs. clean publication report).<br>4. **Interactive Chart Editor:**<br>   * Visualization tabs featuring *Brushing &amp; Linking* (selecting points or bars automatically highlights corresponding cases in Data View).<br>5. **AI Copilot Console (StatCraft Copilot / `statcraft_bridge`):**<br>   * Conversational terminal for executing analyses, data transformations, and natural language interpretation via Model Context Protocol (MCP).</p><h3>4.4. &quot;File&quot; Menu Architecture, StatCraft Projects (.stc), and SPSS (.sav / .zsav) Codecs</h3><p>Upgrading the File menu from a primitive CSV loader into an all-inclusive research lifecycle management hub:</p><p>#### A. Unified Workspace Project Container (`.stc` — StatCraft Project)<br>In classic SPSS, datasets (`.sav`), output logs (`.spv`), and scripts (`.sps`) are fragmented across disconnected files, often severing the link between reports and specific data versions.<br>* **The `.stc` Project Format:** A native, open format built on Apache Parquet and structured JSON metadata, packaging into a single hermetic container:<br>  1. The complete tabular dataset (`DataSet`);<br>  2. The full variable dictionary with rich metadata (`VariableDictionary`: types, measurement scales, `ValueLabels`, user and system missing values `MissingValues`, alignment, column widths, decimal precision);<br>  3. The entire `Output Viewer` workbook (all generated procedures, pivot tables, frequency distributions, `Notes` blocks, and syntax execution history);<br>  4. Application UI layout state and docking topology (`DockState`), restoring the user&#39;s workspace exactly as it was when reopened.</p><p>#### B. Native Support for IBM SPSS Statistics Formats (`.sav` and `.zsav`)<br>Direct opening of SPSS data files without converters or proprietary closed-source libraries (Clean-Room canon on L0 `statcraft_io`):<br>* Binary `.sav` reading conforming to the open GNU PSPP specification;<br>* Streaming decompression of compressed `.zsav` archives using zlib;<br>* Automatic conversion of SPSS variable records into the internal `VariableDictionary` (measurement levels, `SYSMIS` codes, multibyte character encodings);<br>* Export back to `.sav` for seamless round-trip compatibility with SPSS users.</p><p>#### C. Hierarchical Structure of the &quot;File&quot; Menu<br>* **New ▶:**<br>  * New Project (`.stc`) — `Ctrl+Shift+N`;<br>  * New Dataset (Blank Sheet) — `Ctrl+N`;<br>  * Syntax File (`.sps`).<br>* **Open Project (`.stc`)...** — `Ctrl+Shift+O`.<br>* **Open Data (`.sav`, `.zsav`, `.csv`, `.tsv`, `.stc`)...** — `Ctrl+O`.<br>* **Import Data ▶:**<br>  * SPSS Data File (`*.sav`, `*.zsav`)...<br>  * Delimited Text File (CSV, TSV, TXT)...<br>  * Excel Spreadsheet (`*.xlsx`)... (future roadmap).<br>* **Recent Projects &amp; Files ▶:** Fast launch for the last 10 session files with on-disk path history.<br>* **Save Project (`.stc`)** — `Ctrl+S`.<br>* **Save Project As...** — `Ctrl+Shift+S`.<br>* **Save Data As (`.sav`, `.csv`, `.tsv`)...**<br>* **Export ▶:**<br>  * Export Output Workbook (HTML, PDF, TSV)...<br>  * Export Dataset to CSV / Excel...<br>* **Close Project** — `Ctrl+W`.<br>* **Exit** — `Alt+F4`.</p><h3>4.5. &quot;Edit&quot; Menu Architecture</h3><p>The central operational hub for data manipulation, bidirectional command history, and dataset navigation:<br>* **Bidirectional History Stack:**<br>  * Full Undo/Redo (`Ctrl+Z`, `Ctrl+Y` / `Ctrl+Shift+Z`) backed by `CommandBus` for all data grid, variable dictionary, and analysis steps.<br>* **Specialized Clipboard Operations:**<br>  * Cut (`Ctrl+X`), Copy (`Ctrl+C`), Paste (`Ctrl+V`), Clear (`Delete`);<br>  * **Copy with Variable Names (`Ctrl+Shift+C`):** exports selected cells with an auto-generated header row, ready for pasting into external spreadsheets and publication reports.<br>* **High-Capacity Dataset Navigation:**<br>  * **Go to Case (`Ctrl+G`):** instant virtualized scrolling jump to a case by line number (essential for datasets with hundreds of thousands or millions of cases);<br>  * **Go to Variable (`Ctrl+J`):** fuzzy search and column focus by variable name or descriptive label across large questionnaires.<br>* **Grid Search and Replacement:**<br>  * Find (`Ctrl+F`): substring or exact case-sensitive matching across columns;<br>  * Replace (`Ctrl+H`): batch category code and typo replacement.<br>* **Insert Case &amp; Insert Variable:** Insert a new row or column immediately before the active cursor position.<br>* **Options / Preferences Dialog:** Modular environment configuration dialog:<br>  * *Tab 1: General:* UI language (EN/RU), visual theme, recent files limit, session auto-save interval;<br>  * *Tab 2: Data Grid:* decimal separator selection (dot `12.5` vs. comma `12,5`), new variable defaults (width 8, decimals 2), show value labels by default;<br>  * *Tab 3: Fonts &amp; Scale:* table grid font size (9–14 pt), UI scaling factor (100%, 125%, 150% for HiDPI/4K);<br>  * *Tab 4: Output:* pivot table visual style (Classic SPSS, Academic APA), $p$-value styling (`* p &lt; .05`, `** p &lt; .01`);<br>  * *Tab 5: AI &amp; MCP Bridge:* MCP server socket port (18492), dataset access permissions, interpretation verbosity.</p><h3>4.6. &quot;View&quot; Menu Architecture</h3><p>Managing data presentation, visual readability, language switching, and color themes:<br>* **UI Language ▶:** Runtime language switching without restart (`Russian`, `English`, effortlessly extensible by dropping new `.ftl` files into `locales/`).<br>* **Value Labels — `1/A`:** Instant toggling between raw numeric codes and human-readable descriptive category labels (`1` $\leftrightarrow$ `Male`).<br>* **Visual Themes ▶:**<br>  * **Light Theme (Classic SPSS):** traditional light grey/white background with contrast grid lines and blue header accents familiar to SPSS users;<br>  * **Dark Theme (Dark Pro):** modern dark aesthetic engineered to minimize eye strain during long-session analysis;<br>  * **Auto (System):** automatic synchronization with the host Windows OS dark/light mode preference.<br>* **Zoom &amp; Font Size:**<br>  * Rapid table font scaling (`Ctrl++`, `Ctrl+-`, `Ctrl+0`);<br>  * Tailored readability on high-DPI (4K/Retina) displays.<br>* **Grid Lines:** Toggle cell border rendering visibility on the data canvas.<br>* **Status Bar:**<br>  * Displays case count $N$, variable count $P$, and memory footprint;<br>  * Live status flags: active selection filter (`Filter On`), sample weighting (`Weight On`), and file split (`Split File On`).<br>* **Toolbars:** Show/hide the top vector action toolbar.</p><h3>4.7. &quot;Data&quot; Menu Architecture</h3><p>Matrix-level data manipulation, dataset topology, and sample conditioning:<br>* **Sort Cases...:** Multi-level ascending/descending observation sorting across one or multiple variables;<br>* **Sort Variables...:** Reorder columns in data and variable dictionary views by name, type, label, or measurement level;<br>* **Transpose...:** Matrix rotation swapping rows into columns and columns into rows;<br>* **Merge Files ▶:**<br>  * **Add Cases...:** vertical dataset concatenation (combining waves of observations);<br>  * **Add Variables...:** horizontal relational table joining by primary key ID (JOIN / VLOOKUP);<br>* **Restructure...:** Format transformation between Wide (repeated measurements in distinct columns) and Long (time factor and score column) required for repeated-measures ANOVA and mixed models;<br>* **Aggregate...:** Collapsing observation rows with group-level summaries (means, sums, medians);<br>* **Split File...:** Global mode executing all analytical procedures separately per subgroup with live `[Split File On]` status bar flag;<br>* **Select Cases...:** Filtering cases by logical criteria (`Age &gt;= 18 AND Income &gt; 0`) with strikethrough visual masking and `[Filter On]` status bar flag;<br>* **Weight Cases...:** Applying sampling weights to balance representative population margins with `[Weight On]` status bar flag.</p><h3>4.8. &quot;Transform&quot; Menu Architecture — 100% Parity with IBM SPSS Statistics</h3><p>The comprehensive mathematical feature engineering, data imputation, and matrix conditioning toolchain:<br>* **Compute Variable...:** Column formula calculator supporting arithmetic (`SQRT`, `ABS`, `LN`, `EXP`), row-wise statistics (`MEAN`, `SUM`, `SD`, `MIN`, `MAX`), string functions (`CONCAT`, `SUBSTR`), and conditional logical assignments (`IF (condition) Target = expression`);<br>* **Shift Values (Lead &amp; Lag)...:** Time-series lag/lead operators (`LAG(x, 1)`) for autoregressive econometric modeling and rate-of-change calculation;<br>* **Recode ▶:**<br>  * **Recode into Different Variables...:** Non-destructive continuous-to-categorical binning (e.g. age cohorts, income brackets) into a newly minted variable;<br>  * **Recode into Same Variables...:** In-place modification of existing column cells;<br>  * **Automatic Recode...:** Instant alphanumeric text conversion into contiguous integer codes (`1`, `2`) accompanied by automatic generation of dictionary `ValueLabels`;<br>* **Create Dummy Variables...:** Instant transformation of multi-category discrete scales into binary 0/1 indicator columns for multiple regression models;<br>* **Visual Binning...:** Interactive modal featuring a live histogram preview with draggable cut points for slicing variables into equal percentiles, cut points, or standard deviation intervals;<br>* **Optimal Binning...:** Supervised discretization optimizing predictor bin relationships against a categorical target variable;<br>* **Prepare Data for Modeling (ADP)...:** Automated data preparation, anomaly screening, and statistical normalization;<br>* **Rank Cases...:** Order rank calculation with tie handling (Mean, Low, High ties);<br>* **Date and Time Wizard...:** Multi-step wizard for date arithmetic: duration calculation (exact age, tenure), date addition/subtraction, component extraction (day of week, quarter, year);<br>* **Create Time Series...:** Moving averages, exponential smoothing series, and difference transforms to eliminate secular trend;<br>* **Replace Missing Values (Data Imputation)...:** Algorithmic gap filling via Series Mean, Mean of Nearby Points, Median of Nearby Points, Linear Interpolation, or Linear Trend at point;<br>* **Random Number Generators &amp; Seed...:** Pseudorandom seed initialization guaranteeing 100% reproducibility in split-sample validation and Monte Carlo experiments;<br>* **Count Values within Cases...:** Row-wise targeted value occurrence counter (survey battery scales, symptom clusters);<br>* **Programmability Transformations...:** Custom execution of transformation pipelines via the local `statcraft_bridge` socket.</p><h3>4.9. &quot;Analyze&quot; Menu Architecture — 100% Parity with IBM SPSS Statistics</h3><p>The complete inventory of applied statistical procedures organized by canonical thematic submenus:<br>* **Descriptive Statistics ▶:**<br>  * **Frequencies...:** frequency distributions, percentages, valid percentages, cumulative percentages, custom percentiles, quartiles ($Q_1, Q_2, Q_3$);<br>  * **Descriptives...:** mean, standard error, variance, standard deviation, minimum, maximum, range, skewness $G_1$, kurtosis $G_2$;<br>  * **Explore...:** exploratory data analysis (EDA), Boxplots, stem-and-leaf plots, Kolmogorov-Smirnov (with Lilliefors significance correction) and Shapiro-Wilk normality tests;<br>  * **Crosstabs...:** two-way contingency tables, Pearson Chi-Square ($\chi^2$), Fisher&#39;s Exact Test, Yates&#39; continuity correction, association coefficients (Cramér&#39;s $V$, $\phi$, contingency coefficient);<br>* **Compare Means ▶:**<br>  * **One-Sample T Test...:** test sample mean against an external hypothesized parameter $\mu_0$;<br>  * **Independent-Samples T Test...:** two-group mean difference testing, Levene&#39;s test for equality of variances (reporting Student&#39;s $t$ and Welch&#39;s $t$);<br>  * **Paired-Samples T Test...:** dependent matched-pairs / repeated-measures &quot;before-and-after&quot; testing;<br>  * **One-Way ANOVA...:** between-group and within-group variance analysis for $3+$ groups with post-hoc multiple comparisons (Tukey HSD, Bonferroni correction);<br>* **General Linear Model (GLM) ▶:**<br>  * **Univariate (ANCOVA)...:** analysis of covariance conditioning on continuous metric covariates;<br>  * **Multivariate (MANOVA)...:** multivariate analysis of variance evaluating multiple continuous dependent variables simultaneously;<br>  * **Repeated Measures ANOVA...:** longitudinal experimental designs with Mauchly&#39;s test of sphericity;<br>* **Correlate ▶:**<br>  * **Bivariate...:** Pearson product-moment ($r$), Spearman rank-order ($\rho$), and Kendall tau ($\tau$) correlation matrices with two-tailed significance testing;<br>  * **Partial...:** linear association between two variables controlling for the linear effect of one or more additional covariates;<br>* **Regression ▶:**<br>  * **Linear...:** multiple Ordinary Least Squares (OLS) regression, unstandardized $B$ and standardized $\beta$ coefficients, $R^2$, ANOVA $F$-test, collinearity diagnostics (VIF, Tolerance);<br>  * **Binary Logistic...:** dichotomous event probability modeling (0/1), Odds Ratios $\text{Exp}(B)$, Wald test, Hosmer-Lemeshow goodness-of-fit;<br>  * **Multinomial &amp; Ordinal Logistic...:** multi-category unordered and ordered logit modeling;<br>  * **Curve Estimation...:** quadratic, cubic, logarithmic, inverse, and power curve fitting;<br>* **Nonparametric Tests ▶:**<br>  * **Independent Samples:** Mann-Whitney $U$ test (2 groups), Kruskal-Wallis $H$ test ($K$ groups);<br>  * **Related Samples:** Wilcoxon signed-rank test (2 paired conditions), Friedman test ($K$ conditions);<br>* **Dimension Reduction &amp; Classify ▶:**<br>  * **Factor Analysis / PCA...:** sampling adequacy (KMO, Bartlett&#39;s sphericity test), Scree plot eigenvalue extraction, Varimax orthogonal rotation;<br>  * **Cluster Analysis...:** $K$-Means clustering and agglomerative hierarchical clustering with proximity distance matrices and dendrogram visualization;<br>* **Scale &gt; Reliability Analysis...:** Internal consistency evaluation via Cronbach&#39;s Alpha ($\alpha$) and item-deleted scale sensitivity statistics;<br>* **Survival ▶:** Actuarial Life Tables, Kaplan-Meier product-limit survivor curves with Log-Rank tests, Cox Proportional Hazards Regression.</p><h3>4.10. &quot;Direct Marketing&quot; Menu Architecture — Commercial Extension</h3><p>Applied decision-support and customer segmentation toolchain for CRM and commercial marketing analytics (*slated for late-stage implementation following completion of core statistical procedures*):<br>* **RFM Analysis (Recency, Frequency, Monetary)...:** Customer transactional scoring partitioning client databases into actionable tiers (Champions, Loyal, Promising, At Risk, Dormant);<br>* **Profile Potential Contacts...:** Comparative demographic and behavioral profiling identifying characteristics of positive campaign respondents;<br>* **Cluster Analysis for Segmentation...:** Simplified customer clustering wizard tailored for domain marketing practitioners;<br>* **Control Package Test (A/B Testing)...:** Statistical testing verifying significant response rate improvements across campaign variants;<br>* **Postal Code Response Rate...:** Geographic segmentation evaluating localized conversion efficiency across regions.</p><h3>4.11. &quot;Graphs&quot; Menu Architecture — L3 statcraft_charts Vector Engine</h3><p>Interactive scientific visualization engine built on `egui_plot` featuring bidirectional data canvas coupling (Brushing &amp; Linking) and publication-grade vector export:<br>* **Chart Builder...:** Interactive visual canvas featuring a drag-and-drop gallery of graph elements onto coordinate axes ($X$, $Y$) and cluster grouping slots;<br>* **Histogram...:** Continuous distribution plotting with configurable binning intervals and theoretical Gaussian normal curve overlay;<br>* **Bar Chart...:** Simple, clustered, and stacked bar diagrams with 95% confidence interval error bars;<br>* **Boxplot («Box-and-Whisker»)...:** Visualization of medians, interquartile ranges ($IQR$), $1.5 \times IQR$ fences, and labeled outlier observation markers;<br>* **Scatter / Dot Plot...:** Bivariate point clouds with linear regression trendlines and $N \times N$ scatterplot matrices for correlation screening;<br>* **Error Bar...:** Mean comparisons displaying confidence intervals and standard errors;<br>* **Pie Chart...:** Category share proportions with percentage badges;<br>* **Line Chart...:** Longitudinal trajectory and time series trend tracking;<br>* **Population Pyramid...:** Bilateral demographic distribution plots;<br>* **Brushing &amp; Linking Interactivity:** Selecting points or bars on the plot dynamically highlights corresponding records in Data View;<br>* **Vector Graphics Export:** True vector SVG export (ideal for peer-reviewed academic journals without resolution degradation) and high-DPI raster PNG (300+ DPI).</p><h3>4.12. &quot;Utilities&quot; Menu Architecture — Metadata &amp; Questionnaire Structure</h3><p>Dictionary inspection, large-scale questionnaire partitioning, and dataset documentation:<br>* **Variables / Quick Inspector...:** Floating rapid-inspection modal displaying complete metadata for any variable (data type, survey question label, `ValueLabels` table, missing value rules) with a direct cursor focus jump in the active grid without switching tabs;<br>* **Variable Sets (Define &amp; Use)...:** Logical grouping of hundreds of questionnaire items into named domain subsets (&quot;Demographics&quot;, &quot;Depression Scales&quot;, &quot;Financial History&quot;) to filter variable picker lists across all analysis dialogs;<br>* **Data File Comments...:** Embedded research annotation log tracking audit history, cleaning steps, and sample origins stored directly within `.stc` and `.sav` headers;<br>* **Codebook Generator...:** Automatic compilation of a comprehensive study codebook tabulating all dictionary scales, category encodings, and value distributions for documentation and archival handoff.</p><h3>4.13. &quot;Extensions&quot; Menu Architecture — Extensibility, AI MCP &amp; Scripting</h3><p>The open scientific ecosystem bridge integrating external community packages, custom interfaces, and agentic AI models:<br>* **Extension Hub...:** Centralized repository browsing, discovering, and installing community-authored procedure packages with one-click installation;<br>* **Install Local Extension (.scpl)...:** Offline package installer for StatCraft Plugin archives (`.scpl`) adhering to the *Zero-Core Hardcoding* canon;<br>* **Custom Dialog Builder...:** Graphical form designer enabling analysts without low-level Rust experience to construct bespoke dialog modals rendered natively on `egui` and mapped to syntax/Python pipelines;<br>* **AI &amp; Model Context Protocol (MCP) Hub...:** Operational console monitoring the internal MCP server, exposing tools for autonomous orchestration by external AI agents (Antigravity, Claude, local LLMs);<br>* **Scripting Runtime Bridge (Python &amp; R Bridge via `statcraft_bridge`)...:** IPC socket management (18492) and runtime environment path binding for executing custom statistical scripts with safe Arrow memory sharing.</p><h3>4.14. &quot;Window&quot; Menu Architecture — Docking Management &amp; Layout Presets</h3><p>Orchestration of the `egui_dock` multi-document interface, layout safeguards, and split-screen workflows:<br>* **Reset Workspace Layout...:** Panic recovery command restoring default factory topology (Data View on the left, Output Viewer on the right) when panels are accidentally closed or misaligned;<br>* **Layout Presets ▶:**<br>  * *Analysis Preset (Split View):* simultaneous view of the data matrix on the left and live calculation reports on the right;<br>  * *Classic SPSS Preset:* maximized document tabs spanning the entire window frame;<br>  * *Scripting Preset:* horizontal split with Syntax Editor `.sps` on top and Data View below;<br>* **Active Document &amp; View Listing (with direct shortcuts and visibility checks):**<br>  * `[✓] Data View` — `Ctrl+1`;<br>  * `[✓] Variable View` — `Ctrl+2`;<br>  * `[✓] Output Viewer` — `Ctrl+3`;<br>  * `[ ] Syntax Editor` — `Ctrl+4`;<br>  * `[ ] AI Copilot Console` — `Ctrl+5`;<br>* **Minimize All / Restore All Panels.**</p><h3>4.15. &quot;Help&quot; Menu Architecture — Educational Center &amp; Open Science</h3><p>Statistical pedagogy, transparent algorithmic specifications, and onboard sample libraries:<br>* **Statistics Coach &amp; AI Guide...:** Interactive decision tree guiding researchers to appropriate statistical tests based on scale types, sample dimensions, and normality assumptions, offering direct modal launch;<br>* **Mathematical &amp; Algorithm Reference...:** Transparent documentation of the statistical formulas implemented in the L2 `statcraft_algo` core, cross-referenced with peer-reviewed literature and SciPy benchmarks;<br>* **Syntax Reference...:** Language specification and syntax grammar guide for `.sps` script automation;<br>* **Built-in Sample Datasets ▶:** Single-click onboarding datasets:<br>  * Fisher&#39;s Iris Dataset (*iris.csv*);<br>  * Blood Pressure Clinical Trial (*bp_trial.csv*);<br>  * Customer Satisfaction Survey (*survey.csv*);<br>* **Check for Updates...:** Notification and release verification service;<br>* **About StatCraft...:** Application version, dual MIT / Apache-2.0 licensing, repository links, memory safety audit status (100% Safe Rust), and authorship credits.</p><p>---</p><h2>5. Analytical Roadmap Ahead</h2><h3>[x] Phase 6: Compare Means &amp; Hypothesis Testing</h3><p>* **One-Sample T-Test:**<br>  * Compares sample mean against hypothesized test value $\mu_0$;<br>  * $t$-statistic, degrees of freedom $df$, two-tailed $p$-value, 95% confidence interval of the difference.<br>* **Independent-Samples T-Test:**<br>  * Levene&#39;s Test for Equality of Variances ($F$-statistic and $p$-value);<br>  * Student&#39;s $t$-test (equal variances assumed) and Welch&#39;s $t$-test (equal variances not assumed);<br>  * Grouping variable and group definition dialog.<br>* **Paired-Samples T-Test:**<br>  * Repeated measures / paired observations, pair correlation, difference $t$-statistic.<br>* **One-Way ANOVA:**<br>  * Between-group and within-group Sum of Squares ($SS$), Mean Squares ($MS$), Fisher&#39;s $F$-test;<br>  * Post-Hoc Tests: Tukey HSD, Bonferroni correction.</p><h3>[ ] Phase 7: Association Analysis &amp; Non-Parametric Tests</h3><p>* **Crosstabulations (Crosstabs):**<br>  * Two-way contingency tables for nominal/ordinal scales;<br>  * Observed and expected counts, row/column/total percentages;<br>  * Pearson Chi-Square ($\chi^2$), Yates&#39; continuity correction, Fisher&#39;s Exact Test ($2 \times 2$);<br>  * Directional and symmetric measures: Pearson contingency coefficient, Cramér&#39;s $V$, $\phi$.<br>* **Bivariate Correlations:**<br>  * Pearson linear correlation ($r$);<br>  * Spearman ($\rho$) and Kendall ($\tau$) rank correlations;<br>  * Correlation matrix with significance stars ($* p &lt; 0.05$, $** p &lt; 0.01$).<br>* **Non-Parametric Tests:**<br>  * Mann-Whitney $U$ test (independent two-group alternative);<br>  * Wilcoxon signed-rank test (paired samples alternative);<br>  * Kruskal-Wallis $H$ test (one-way ANOVA alternative).</p><h3>[ ] Phase 8: Data Manipulation &amp; Transformation</h3><p>* **Compute Variable:**<br>  * Built-in safe expression parser (`TARGET = VAR_A + SQRT(VAR_B)`);<br>  * Mathematical, statistical, and conditional functions (`SUM`, `MEAN`, `ABS`, `LN`, `EXP`, `IF`);<br>  * Calculator dialog with function palette and variable selector.<br>* **Recode:**<br>  * «Recode into Same Variables» and «Recode into Different Variables»;<br>  * Range mapping interface (`1 thru 18 -&gt; 1`, `19 thru 65 -&gt; 2`, `ELSE -&gt; Copy`).<br>* **Data Management:**<br>  * Sort Cases by multiple keys (ascending/descending);<br>  * Select Cases (filtering observations by logical condition);<br>  * Merge Files (add cases or add variables by key).</p><h3>[ ] Phase 9: Statistical Graphics &amp; Visualization</h3><p>* **Vector Plotting Engine (`egui_plot`):**<br>  * **Histogram:** configurable bin widths, superimposed normal curve;<br>  * **Bar Chart:** simple, clustered, stacked bars with 95% error bars;<br>  * **Boxplot:** median, IQR box, 1.5 IQR whiskers, outlier markers;<br>  * **Scatter Plot:** 2D point cloud with linear regression fit line;<br>  * **Pie Chart:** categorical share breakdown.<br>* **Brushing &amp; Linking:**<br>  * Selecting data points in a chart automatically highlights corresponding rows in Data View.<br>* **High-Resolution Vector Export:** SVG and PNG export.</p><h3>[ ] Phase 10: Regression &amp; Multivariate Analytics</h3><p>* **Linear Regression:**<br>  * Ordinary Least Squares (OLS);<br>  * Coefficients ($B$, $SE_B$, standardized $\beta$, $t$-statistic, $p$-value);<br>  * Model summary: $R$, $R^2$, adjusted $R^2$, ANOVA $F$;<br>  * Multicollinearity diagnostics (VIF, Tolerance).<br>* **Binary Logistic Regression:**<br>  * Maximum likelihood estimation;<br>  * Odds Ratios ($\text{Exp}(B)$), Wald test, pseudo-$R^2$ (Cox &amp; Snell, Nagelkerke).<br>* **Principal Component Analysis (PCA / Factor Analysis):**<br>  * KMO sample adequacy and Bartlett&#39;s test of sphericity;<br>  * Eigenvalue extraction ($\lambda &gt; 1$) and scree plot;<br>  * Varimax orthogonal rotation.<br>* **Reliability Analysis:**<br>  * Cronbach&#39;s Alpha ($\alpha$) for scale internal consistency;<br>  * Item-total statistics (alpha if item deleted).<br>* **Cluster Analysis:**<br>  * $K$-Means clustering;<br>  * Hierarchical clustering with dendrogram.</p><h3>[ ] Phase 11: File Codecs &amp; Reporting</h3><p>* **IBM SPSS `.sav` and `.zsav` Codec:**<br>  * Native clean-room read/write support without proprietary DLLs;<br>  * Full preservation of metadata: variable labels, value labels, measure scales, missing values (`SYSMIS`);<br>  * Support for compressed `.zsav`.<br>* **StatCraft Native Project Codec `.stc`:**<br>  * High-performance columnar storage based on Apache Parquet and JSON metadata.<br>* **Document Export:**<br>  * Export Output Viewer books into PDF, Word DOCX, LaTeX, HTML, and Excel (`.xlsx`).</p><h3>[ ] Phase 12: Syntax Engine &amp; AI Ecosystem</h3><p>* **Interactive Syntax Editor:**<br>  * Dedicated script workspace for SPSS syntax (`.sps`);<br>  * Syntax highlighting, line numbers, autocomplete;<br>  * `Paste` button in all dialogs emits syntax directly into editor.<br>* **Built-in Model Context Protocol (MCP) Server:**<br>  * Connect external AI agents (Antigravity, Claude, local LLMs) directly to running StatCraft;<br>  * MCP tools: inspect dictionary, execute analyses, stream natural language interpretations directly into Output Viewer.<br>* **StatCraft CLI:**<br>  * Headless runner for automated batch pipelines: `statcraft-cli --run script.sps --output report.html`.</p><h3>[ ] Phase 13: Advanced &amp; Specialty Modules</h3><p>* **Survival Analysis (Biostatistics &amp; Medical Science):**<br>  * Life Tables analysis;<br>  * Kaplan-Meier estimation with Log-Rank, Breslow, and Tarone-Ware tests;<br>  * Cox Proportional Hazards Regression with time-dependent covariates.<br>* **Time Series &amp; Forecasting:**<br>  * Autoregressive Integrated Moving Average (*ARIMA / SARIMA*);<br>  * Exponential Smoothing (Single, Holt linear, Winters seasonal);<br>  * Autocorrelation and Partial Autocorrelation Functions (ACF / PACF);<br>  * Unit root / Stationarity tests (Augmented Dickey-Fuller ADF).<br>* **Generalized Linear Models (GLM / GENLIN):**<br>  * Poisson Regression for count and rare event data;<br>  * Negative Binomial Regression for overdispersed count data;<br>  * Gamma Regression and Inverse Gaussian models.<br>* **Linear Mixed Models (LMM):**<br>  * Hierarchical Linear Models (HLM) for multi-level data;<br>  * Repeated Measures ANOVA with random intercepts and slopes;<br>  * Flexible residual covariance structures (Auto-regressive AR(1), Compound Symmetry, Unstructured).<br>* **Complex Samples Analysis:**<br>  * Multi-stage stratified and clustered sample survey analysis;<br>  * Sampling weight adjustments with Taylor series variance estimation.<br>* **Specialized Marketing &amp; Social Research Procedures:**<br>  * Multidimensional Scaling (*PROXSCAL / ALSCAL*);<br>  * Simple and Multiple Correspondence Analysis;<br>  * Conjoint Analysis;<br>  * Decision &amp; Classification Trees (*CHAID, Exhaustive CHAID, CRT, QUEST*).</p><p>---</p><h2>5. Quality Assurance &amp; Definition of Done</h2><p>Every roadmap feature is committed strictly when satisfying:<br>1. **Resource Guard:** `-j 1` on all cargo commands.<br>2. **100% Test Pass:** 0 failures, Golden Oracle precision $\le 10^{-6}$.<br>3. **i18n Linter:** 0 hardcoded strings in UI.<br>4. **Layer Integrity:** `cargo xtask layers` passes.<br>5. **Clean Linters:** `cargo clippy --workspace -j 1 -- -D warnings` and `cargo fmt --check`.<br>6. **Bilingual Chronicle:** Synchronous entries in `docs/CHRONICLE.md` and `docs/CHRONICLE.en.md`.</p><hr><p style="color:#8a8175;font-size:12px">Exported from CapsuleCraft Native · &lt;doc-statcraft-docs_roadmap_en_md@capsuleos.local&gt;</p></body></html>

